From 1fa54fc73b5c75bb823a044d84898c1f84674d79 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 22:55:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] PredicateCompiler: monomial pass for exact predicates on
 doubles of any exponent

A 'dpredicate Name(points) inputs xy|xyz' entry is a homogeneous polynomial in double
coordinates (the determinant with a column of ones). The pass (Monomials.cs) expands it into
its monomials, derives the limbs of two fixed-point accumulators for every exponent span and
generates a kernel that adds the exact mantissa products at their exponents and compares the
accumulators: integer arithmetic only, no allocation, no range restriction.

doubles.spec holds Orient2d, Orient3d and InCircle (6 / 24 / 48 monomials of degree 2 / 3 / 4;
66 / 99 / 132 limbs at the largest span of two doubles); math/Generated/DoublePredicates.cs is
the checked-in output, docs/design/EXACT_FALLBACK_MONOMIALS.md the design note with the
generated table. GeneratedDoublePredicatesTests keeps both equal to the generator, checks the
limb rule with exact integers for every span, the kernels against the BigInteger determinants
and the helper of one monomial against BigInteger on accumulators with long carries.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
